## The Code Trail — 7 Files, End to End

### 1️⃣ The Hardware Interface — configfs-tsm

[`packages/agent/src/quote-provider.ts`](file:///c:/Users/Gupta/OneDrive/Desktop/rime/packages/agent/src/quote-provider.ts)

This is where the rubber meets the road. `ConfigfsTsmQuoteProvider` talks directly to the Linux kernel's TDX attestation interface — no SDK wrapper, no simulator:

```typescript
// Line 28-68: The real hardware interface
export class ConfigfsTsmQuoteProvider {
  constructor(basePath = "/sys/kernel/config/tsm/report") { ... }

  async getQuote(reportData: Hex): Promise<QuoteResult> {
    // Write 64 bytes of report_data to the kernel
    await writeFile(path.join(entryDir, "inblob"), bytes);
    // Read the hardware-signed quote back
    const quoteBytes = await readFile(path.join(entryDir, "outblob"));
  }
}
```

**Key point for demo:** This path (`/sys/kernel/config/tsm/report`) only exists on a real TDX guest VM. It doesn't exist on regular machines — `mkdir` would fail with ENOENT, making it impossible to fake.

